# GoThru 3D — Frontend Auth & Persistence: Non-Technical Overview

**What this covers:** How users sign in, stay signed in, and how their work is automatically saved as they use the app.

---

## Pages and What They Do

| Page | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/register` | New users create an account |
| `/login` | Returning users sign in |
| `/verify-email-pending` | Shown right after signup — tells the user to check their inbox |
| `/verify-email` | The landing page when a user clicks the link in their verification email |
| `/forgot-password` | User requests a password reset link by email |
| `/reset-password` | User sets a new password after clicking the reset link |
| `/dashboard` | Overview of all the user's projects — rename, delete, publish |
| `/start` | Step-by-step wizard to create a new project |
| `/editor` | The 3D floor plan editor, with auto-save |

---

## Signing In

1. User enters their email and password on `/login`
2. If the credentials are correct and the email is verified, they're taken to the dashboard
3. If the email isn't verified yet, they're redirected to the verification pending page with guidance
4. Once signed in, the session is kept securely — the user stays logged in across page refreshes and browser sessions until they explicitly log out

---

## Registering a New Account

1. User fills in their name, email, and password on `/register`
2. The system creates the account and immediately signs them in
3. They're redirected to the "check your email" page (`/verify-email-pending`)
4. They cannot access the project wizard or editor until their email is verified

---

## Email Verification Flow

```
Sign up → "Check your email" page → Click link in email → Verified ✓ → Redirected to app
```

- If the link has expired (older than 24 hours), the user can request a new one from the pending page
- After successful verification, the signed-in session is automatically updated so the app immediately knows the user is verified — no need to log out and back in

---

## Forgot Password Flow

```
/forgot-password → Enter email → Email sent → Click link → /reset-password → Set new password → Done
```

- The page always says "email sent" regardless of whether the address is in the system (protects user privacy)
- The reset link is valid for 1 hour and can only be used once

---

## Access Control (Who Can See What)

| Page / Area | Who can access it |
|-------------|-------------------|
| `/login`, `/register`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password` | Everyone (no sign-in required) |
| `/dashboard` | Signed-in users (email verification not required here — so they can still resend the verification email) |
| `/start` (project wizard) | Signed-in users **with** a verified email |
| `/editor` | Signed-in users **with** a verified email |

If an unauthenticated user tries to visit a protected page, they're automatically redirected to `/login`. If a signed-in but unverified user tries to access the wizard or editor, they're redirected to `/verify-email-pending`.

---

## How Work Gets Saved

GoThru saves the user's work automatically at multiple points:

### Creating a Project (Wizard)

| Wizard Step | What Gets Saved |
|-------------|-----------------|
| Step 1 confirmed (name + location) | Project created in the database |
| Step 3 → Step 4 (floor configuration done) | Floor settings saved to the project |
| Scan complete | AI-generated 3D model saved; project status updated to "scanned" |

### In the Editor

- **Auto-save:** 2 seconds after the user stops making changes, their work is saved automatically
- **Manual save:** A save button is always available for users who prefer to save explicitly
- **Offline fallback:** If saving fails due to a network issue, the data is temporarily kept in the browser and re-attempted — the user doesn't lose work
- A "Saving…" indicator and a "Last saved at [time]" stamp are shown in the editor toolbar

### Restoring Work

When a user returns to the app, their most recently active project is automatically restored from the database — no need to navigate back to it manually.

---

## File Uploads

When a user uploads a floor plan image:

```
User's browser → GoThru website → GoThru file storage
```

The upload goes through the GoThru website (not directly to storage), so the website can verify the user is logged in and authorised before accepting the file. The user never interacts with the storage system directly.

---

## Logging Out

- Clicking "Sign out" clears the session immediately
- The user is redirected to the login page
- Any locally stored session data is cleaned up

---

## Billing & Subscription

Users can manage their GoThru subscription from a dedicated billing page. No payment details are ever handled by the GoThru website — all sensitive checkout and payment management is hosted by Stripe.

### Pages

| Page | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/billing` | Shows current subscription status and a Subscribe or Manage button |
| `/billing/success` | Shown after a successful Stripe payment — confirms the subscription and redirects to dashboard after 3 seconds |
| `/billing/cancel` | Shown when a user cancels out of the Stripe checkout — no charge was made |

### Subscribing (First Time)

1. User visits `/billing` — the page loads their current subscription status from the backend
2. If no active subscription exists, a "Subscribe" button is shown
3. Clicking "Subscribe" asks the GoThru backend to create a Stripe Checkout Session
4. The browser is redirected to Stripe's hosted payment page
5. After payment, Stripe redirects the user to `/billing/success`
6. The backend receives a webhook from Stripe and marks the subscription as active

### Managing an Existing Subscription

1. User visits `/billing` — status shows "active" and the renewal date
2. Clicking "Manage subscription" asks the backend to open the Stripe Billing Portal
3. The browser is redirected to Stripe's hosted portal
4. After making changes, Stripe redirects the user back to `/billing`

### Subscription Status Labels

| Status | What the user sees |
|--------|--------------------|
| **active** | "Your subscription is active" with renewal date |
| **past_due** | "Your subscription payment is past due" + Subscribe button |
| **canceled** | "Your subscription has been canceled" + Subscribe button |
| **inactive** | "You don't have an active subscription" + Subscribe button |

---

## Environment Configuration

The frontend requires the following settings to be configured:

| Setting | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| NextAuth URL | The public URL of the website (e.g. https://app.gothru.co) — also used by Stripe as the base for billing redirect URLs |
| NextAuth secret | A strong random key used to encrypt the session cookie (32+ characters) |
| API URL | The internal address of the GoThru backend service (never exposed to the browser) |
